{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T19:31:41-07:00","id":640991,"title":"","content":"Woo!<br /> <br /> Love it. I'll have to finish that mummy friend for Yaritza Ramirez.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T22:40:04-07:00","id":641152,"title":"","content":"At least! Now I need to decide if to move <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/640622-beast-vampire-sas-%E2%80%98morning-after%E2%80%99-%E2%80%93-actual-play\">Beast &amp; Vampire 'Morning After' SAS Actual Play</a> in general WoD or in to Beast forum - part of it's reason as to test crossover capabilities of game. Any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T03:20:28-07:00","id":641319,"title":"","content":"Since this is a thing now, where would one go to get an introduction to Beast that's written for people who already know what RPGs and the WoD are?<br /> <br /> I am aware there is apparently an extensive preview floating somewhere, which is approaching being the entire text of the book, which I don't want to read, because I want to read the thing with finished layout and stuff. But the preview blurps are very insubstantial, and barely even register as a teaser.<br /> <br /> Is there anywhere, where I could find an introduction that tells me what Beast is actually about? And I don't mean telling me that it's a game <i>about Primordial hunger</i>, I mean something that would actually provide information to someone who's played other WoD games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T05:58:34-07:00","id":641439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/640853-welcome-to-the-beast-forum?p=641319#post641319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since this is a thing now, where would one go to get an introduction to Beast that's written for people who already know what RPGs and the WoD are?<br /> <br /> I am aware there is apparently an extensive preview floating somewhere, which is approaching being the entire text of the book, which I don't want to read, because I want to read the thing with finished layout and stuff. But the preview blurps are very insubstantial, and barely even register as a teaser.<br /> <br /> Is there anywhere, where I could find an introduction that tells me what Beast is actually about? And I don't mean telling me that it's a game <i>about Primordial hunger</i>, I mean something that would actually provide information to someone who's played other WoD games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is just the Introduction chapter from the Kickstarter Preview not good enough?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T06:51:56-07:00","id":641468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/640853-welcome-to-the-beast-forum?p=641319#post641319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anywhere, where I could find an introduction that tells me what Beast is actually about? And I don't mean telling me that it's a game <i>about Primordial hunger</i>, I mean something that would actually provide information to someone who's played other WoD games.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Primordial Dream is a region of the Astral real (the same one mages sometimes visit) where fears coalesce - including symbolic nightmare monsters called Horrors. Beasts are people born with a connection to one of these Horrors - eventually there's a &quot;big day&quot; where they merge with it fully and it replaces their soul - this might happen spontaneously, or it might be facilitated by another Beast.<br /> <br /> Beasts have to keep their horror fed, which is about sating a constant hunger (to hoard, to dominate, to hunt, to punish, or to destroy). It's possible to do this more or less harmlessly, but that's only small meals - it's possible to stick to those who seem deserving in some fashion, but that's unreliable meals - and hunger is uncomfortable, not to mention that if it gets hungry enough, the Horror will go rampaging through the dreamscape feeding itself. So part of the game is finding a feeding balance you can live with. Feeding is usually through relatively ordinary actions, so it's a good game for exploring undercurrents of evil, power, and the abuse of power in ordinary life.<br /> <br /> Beasts encourage each other to be teachers of a sort. Their own nightmares of the Primordial Dream tended to provoke insight, and they think they can do the same to/for humans. It's a good way of living with yourself, at least.<br /> <br /> Beast is also about family. They claim to be descended from a &quot;Dark Mother,&quot; and also that most other supernaturals are their cousins descended from her too (there is no proof of this in the game, though Beasts can form bonds of kinship with supernatural beings, empowering both parties in various ways). Beasts seek out relationships inside and outside their species - in that sense, it's a game designed to encourage crossover - though you don't <i>need</i> to include other supernaturals. But they are explorers and busybodies, so some other supernatural weirdness beyond them is helpful.<br /> <br /> Beasts have to beware of Heroes, who are people born with their own, more hostile, connection to the Primordial Dream. When they come across Beasts, that connection rises up and fills them with a need (and power) to hunt Beasts. There's a narrative vibe to this: a Beast/Hero battle is a contest of &quot;Who's story is this really,&quot; as much as a physical one. Heroes can be tragic figures as well, and a lot of Beasts need killing - but most Heroes are undiscriminating killers, and a lot of Beasts <i>don't</i> need killing - neither side is good at seeing nuance in the other.<br /> <br /> Beasts are powerful; this is a high-power game. Despite this, it's oddly suited to having its protagonists live like regular people (even they have one foot in a the secret supernatural world around them).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T23:38:30-07:00","id":642666,"title":"","content":"Thanks, this helped me a lot more than the KS introduction did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T00:11:00-07:00","id":642708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/640853-welcome-to-the-beast-forum?p=642666#post642666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, this helped me a lot more than the KS introduction did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there were a few changes from when that introduction was written and now. I mean originally Heroes were all without exception amoral psychopaths in a situation where you could argue that they're suffering a mental illness with decent backing. Now its at least acknowledged less psychotic ones exist, but the Heroes who go on to work projects and use therapy to help the victims of Beast attacks make for less interesting antagonists than the ones that want to destroy the Beast and everything it's made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/co